# request: "Architecture diagram of our shop platform for the README. Web and mobile
#  clients call a Kong API gateway, which routes REST calls to the Catalog, Orders and
#  Payments services. Catalog and Orders use the Postgres shop DB. Orders publishes
#  order events to Kafka; the Notifications worker consumes them and emails
#  customers through SendGrid. Payments charges cards with Stripe. Highlight Orders."
type: architecture
reader: GitHub README
width: 800
direction: down
focus: services.orders  # "Highlight Orders"
out: admin UI, observability, CI/CD, languages of the services (not given)
nodes:
  web: Web client
  mobile: Mobile client
  gateway: API gateway\nKong
  events: Order events\nKafka {shape: queue}
  services: Services
  services.payments: Payments
  services.catalog: Catalog
  services.orders: Orders
  services.notify: Notifications
  data: Data and third parties
  data.stripe: Stripe\ncard payments {external}
  data.db: Shop DB\nPostgres {shape: cylinder}
  data.sendgrid: SendGrid\nemail {external}
edges:
  web -> gateway
  mobile -> gateway
  gateway -> services.payments: REST
  gateway -> services.catalog: REST
  gateway -> services.orders: REST
  services.orders -> events: publishes {dashed}
  events -> services.notify: consumes {dashed}
  services.payments -> data.stripe: charges
  services.catalog -> data.db: uses
  services.orders -> data.db: uses
  services.notify -> data.sendgrid: sends email
